  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilience and Addressing Vulnerability to Emergencies (BRAVE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">British High Commission (BHC) in Pakistan, through its Foreign, Commonwealth, and Development Office (FCDO) is implementing a &#xA3;97 million programme, the &#x2018;Building Resilience and Addressing Vulnerability to Emergencies&#x2019; (BRAVE) in Pakistan. The programme sits within its Climate, Resilience and Humanitarian Group. The BRAVE programme aims to maximise the Government of Pakistan (GoP) and communities&#x2019; capacity to build resilience and adapt to climate related shocks and stresses, including support for adaptive and shock responsive social protection systems. The programme will also help respond to new and ongoing critical humanitarian emergencies within the scope of the Humanitarian Country Teams (HCT) coordinated response(s) or Humanitarian Response Plans/Appeals.</narrative>
  </description>
